From 83bd09e05ddedb7fb52ad0aa000b00bcb5f4d141 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 18 Aug 2026 11:37:08 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Hide pending state, scale the social row to the links that
 exist
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Three changes to the place detail page.

Pending submissions are now invisible. A field awaiting review renders
exactly as if nothing were there — no "under review" badge — but it is
also not offered for input: it is dropped from the picker, and a value
with a queued correction loses its pencil. So nobody can resubmit
thinking it failed, and a second person cannot queue a competing value.
When a section has nothing to show and nothing to offer it removes
itself rather than leave a heading over empty space.

The social row now sizes itself to the number of real links. One link
gets a full-width tile laid out horizontally instead of a third of a row
with two gaps beside it; two get halves; three get thirds. The remaining
platforms move out of the grid into the same quiet text link used by the
all-empty state, so a place with only a Telegram group keeps the focus
on that link rather than on two blanks.

The sheet no longer focuses its field on open. Auto-focus threw the
on-screen keyboard up before the user had read what was being asked for;
they now tap the field when ready.
